  "question": {
    "text": "Let $I(x)=\\int \\frac{6}{\\sin ^2 x(1-\\cot x)^2} d x$. If $I(0)=3$, then $I\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "1e3FU",
      "text": "$2 \\sqrt{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "RGF9R",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ilum9",
      "text": "$3 \\sqrt{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "YmN4g",
      "text": "$6 \\sqrt{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$I(x)=\\int \\frac{6 d x}{\\sin ^2 x(1-\\cot x)^2}=\\int \\frac{6 \\operatorname{cosec}^2 x d x}{(1-\\cot x)^2}$<br />Put $1-\\cot x=t$\n$\\operatorname{cosec}^2 \\mathrm{xdx}=\\mathrm{dt}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & I=\\int \\frac{6 d t}{t^2}=\\frac{-6}{t}+c \\\\ & I(x)=\\frac{-6}{1-\\cot x} c, c=3 \\\\ & I(x)=3-\\frac{6}{1-\\cot x}, I\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)=3-\\frac{6}{1-(2+\\sqrt{3})} \\\\ & I\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)=3+\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{3}+1}=3+\\frac{6(\\sqrt{3}-1)}{2}=3 \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
